522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 230 0 R
/T (A Thermal Power Station \(TPS\) is a power generation plant in which electrical energy is produced by converting thermal energy into mechanical energy and then into electrical energy. In a TPS, heat energy obtained from the combustion of fuel such as coal, oil, or gas is used to generate steam. This steam drives a turbine, which in turn rotates an alternator to produce electricity. TPS form the backbone of electric power generation in many countries due to their reliability, ability to generate large amounts of power, and continuous operation. These plants are widely used to meet base load and peak load demands of industries and utilities. TPS consist of major components such as intake system, water treatment plant, DM plant, boiler, steam turbine, generator, condenser, cooling system, and transformers. Efficient operation and maintenance of these systems ensure reliable power generation with high efficiency and safety. Due to their capability to operate continuously and support large electrical loads, thermal power stations are extensively used in refineries, power plants, and large industrial complexes.)
/E (A Thermal Power Station \(TPS\) is a power generation plant in which electrical energy is produced by converting thermal energy into mechanical energy and then into electrical energy. In a TPS, heat energy obtained from the combustion of fuel such as coal, oil, or gas is used to generate steam. This steam drives a turbine, which in turn rotates an alternator to produce electricity. TPS form the backbone of electric power generation in many countries due to their reliability, ability to generate large amounts of power, and continuous operation. These plants are widely used to meet base load and peak load demands of industries and utilities. TPS consist of major components such as intake system, water treatment plant, DM plant, boiler, steam turbine, generator, condenser, cooling system, and transformers. Efficient operation and maintenance of these systems ensure reliable power generation with high efficiency and safety. Due to their capability to operate continuously and support large electrical loads, thermal power stations are extensively used in refineries, power plants, and large industrial complexes.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2 3 4 5]
>>
