978 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (Pole slip protection safeguards synchronous generators against loss of synchronism with the power system. During pole slip, the rotor no longer rotates in synchronism with the stator magnetic field, leading to severe mechanical and electrical stresses.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
979 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (The protection operates by monitoring the impedance trajectory at the generator terminals. During loss of synchronism, the impedance moves in a characteristic path on the R-X plane. When this trajectory crosses predefined relay zones within a specified time, pole slip is detected.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
