1019 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 256 0 R
/T (An Air Circuit Breaker \(ACB\) operates by interrupting the circuit through contacts placed in open air. When a fault occurs and the contacts separate, an arc is formed which is divided into several smaller arcs by an arc chute. These smaller arcs are then quickly extinguished due to the cooling effect of air and electromagnetic forces. ACBs are generally used in low-voltage applications and are commonly installed for systems operating in the voltage range of 380V to 480V. They provide effective protection against overcurrent, short-circuit, and ground faults in industrial installations like Guwahati Refinery.)
/E (An Air Circuit Breaker \(ACB\) operates by interrupting the circuit through contacts placed in open air. When a fault occurs and the contacts separate, an arc is formed which is divided into several smaller arcs by an arc chute. These smaller arcs are then quickly extinguished due to the cooling effect of air and electromagnetic forces. ACBs are generally used in low-voltage applications and are commonly installed for systems operating in the voltage range of 380V to 480V. They provide effective protection against overcurrent, short-circuit, and ground faults in industrial installations like Guwahati Refinery.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
